      "side": 1,
      "message": "NIIICE!!! Sounds like more linux-on-linux CI testing coming soon? 😊 \n\nMostly just one large comment/discussion on naming and location:\n\nCould these be renamed to `kumquat_\u003cfunction\u003e` and `kumquat_\u003cstruct\u003e` and this subdirectory to `hardware/google/gfxstream/guest/platform/kumquat`? The `rutabaga_` prefix does not help a reader distinguish between these new functions and the existing `rutabaga_` variants. I suppose a prefix of `kumquat_rutabaga_` would also work as this suggested to the reader that the `kumquat` impl forwards things to the `rutabaga` layer but I suppose even that is an implementation detail. The `virtgpu_` part does not really add much detail outside of everything being related to gpu emulation. Similarly, the `drm_` prefix seems unused as these structs are never actually sent across the drm layer.\n\nOn a related note (since the defines are shared there and here), could crrev.com/c/5645904 potentially be restructured to be `rutabaga_gfx/kumquat/server` and `rutabaga_gfx/kumquat/client` with all of the existing `rutabaga_gfx/virtgpu_rutabaga` code moved into the `client` subdirectory?",
